Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: a game can name what the Resolution row's Auto means (PS2X_GPU_SCALE_AUTO_LABEL)

With a renderer of its own that draws at the screen's size, "Auto (2560 x 1344)" (the emulated picture's size) misled.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_settings_panel.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_settings_panel.cpp
@@ -992,6 +992,13 @@
             std::vector<Choice> list = choices();
             int x = 0, y = 0;
             ps2_gpu::scale(x, y);
+            // (A game whose own renderer draws the picture at the screen's size can name what Auto means there:
+            // PS2X_GPU_SCALE_AUTO_LABEL. Otherwise Auto shows the emulated picture's size it chose.)
+            if (const char *own = std::getenv("PS2X_GPU_SCALE_AUTO_LABEL"); own && *own)
+            {
+                list.front().label = own;
+                return list;
+            }
             if (autoAtStart && x > 0 && y > 0 && ps2_gpu::requested())
             {
                 char label[64];
